 to keep T1, T2, T7, T8, T9, and W1 (at least one), and get T3.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to discard a tile that's not needed for this pattern. B1 is the best candidate. So the answer is to play B1.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [The best move is to discard B1 to preserve the potential for forming a Mixed Straight by collecting T3 and keeping T1, T2, T7, T8, T9.]\nReason: [Discarding B1, a terminal tile not critical to the Mixed Straight pattern, allows focusing on completing the required Chows (1-2-3 and 7-8-9) while retaining key tiles (T1, T2, T7, T8, T9) and a pair of W1. This maximizes the chance of achieving an 8-point Mixed Straight.]\nAnswer: Play B1"}
